# punused findings adjudicated for this repo. One literal substring per line,
# matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the reason.
# This LIBRARY ships a `main` package (internal/e2etestserver), so CI's app-mode
# detection runs punused on it, but its exported surface is a PUBLISHED Go API
# consumed by marotte, web-terminal-kiro and web-terminal-server. punused sees no
# references from outside the module, so nothing is deleted on its word. EU1001 vs
# EU1002 says only whether THIS repo's tests exercise a symbol. Patterns are
# symbol-only (no file:line) so they survive line shifts.

# --- Session-manager surface: published API, consumers web-terminal-kiro and
# web-terminal-server. The calls live in another MODULE, invisible to punused.
#
# NewSessionManager / WithManagerLogger / WithStatusClassifier: built at
# web-terminal-kiro/routes.go and web-terminal-server/main.go.
# MountAPI + WithCreateGate: web-terminal-kiro/routes.go mounts the session
# REST API behind a create gate; web-terminal-server/main.go does the same
# with webhttp.SessionCreateRateLimit.
# WithIdleReaper: web-terminal-server/main.go only (kiro runs no reaper).
# (*SessionManager).Shutdown: drains every session on SIGTERM through
# webhttp.Run's shutdown hook -- web-terminal-kiro/main.go,
# web-terminal-server/main.go.
# (*SessionManager).Create: the id-only public form of session creation, kept as
# published API. From v3.9.0 this repo's own REST handler calls the unexported
# create() instead, because handleCreate echoes the full SessionInfo it stored
# rather than re-deriving it, so Create reads as test-only here. Deleting an
# exported method of a published v3 module would be a semver-major break.
# (*SessionManager).StatusLatch / WithdrawStatusLatch: the compare-and-swap pair
# web-terminal-kiro's pending-interaction poller uses to clear a needs-input
# latch once kiro-cli's own record shows the ask settled (nothing on the PTY
# byte stream reports that falling edge). Covered in-repo by
# terminal/status_latch_test.go; the production caller is in another MODULE.
function NewSessionManager
function WithManagerLogger
function WithStatusClassifier
function WithCreateGate
function WithIdleReaper
method (*SessionManager).MountAPI
method (*SessionManager).Shutdown
method (*SessionManager).Create
method (*SessionManager).StatusLatch
method (*SessionManager).WithdrawStatusLatch

