# (*Handler).Shutdown (terminal/terminal.go) -- EU1001, and the "test only" here
# is a DESIGN consequence rather than a gap. Shutdown is Close plus the wait, and
# the engine's own SessionManager deliberately does not use it: it calls Close on
# every session FIRST and waits on each afterwards (terminal/session_manager.go,
# Shutdown), so the sessions' teardown windows overlap inside one budget instead
# of summing. Routing the manager through this method would serialize them, which
# is the behavior it exists to avoid, so wiring it up in-repo would be a
# regression rather than a fix.
#
# The consumer it is published for holds a bare Handler with no manager in front
# of it: marotte/internal/agent/shell.go's ShellManager, which owns one PTY for the
# built-in shell. web-terminal-kiro and web-terminal-server reach the wait through
# SessionManager.Shutdown instead.
#
# Covered in-repo by terminal/shutdown_test.go (TestShutdownWaitsForTeardown,
# TestShutdownReportsAnExpiredBudget, TestShutdownOnAnUnstartedHandlerReturnsNil,
# TestShutdownReportsSuccessAfterCompletion), each red-checked against a mutant.
method (*Handler).Shutdown
